  "statement": "On 3 of 5 household-days this page shows, the company's own grid shape can be checked against NESO's published series. It overstates the timing effect on 2 of them, by 1.7 percentage points on average and 4.6 at the widest, and on 1 the two disagree about whether the household drew cleaner or dirtier than average at all. The company is not shown the published series and is not corrected by it: the gap IS the score."
